{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/947102-life-4-attinument","id":947102,"title":"Life 4 Attinument","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T11:04:48-07:00","id":947102,"title":"Life 4 Attinument","content":"Hi Guys! Nice to be on the &quot;posting side&quot; of the forum for a change <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I`ll be brief.<br /> The life 4 Attinument says that any supernatural power that will injure the life mage, will trigger a Clash of Will.<br /> <br /> The Attinuemnt says also that the clash is applicable when the Mage`s body is modified in some way.<br /> <br /> Do you think that any direct damage spell ( like the Arcana 3 and 4 ones ) will trigger this Clash of Will? Or do you think that only magical effect that produce a damage effect, activly modfying the target`s body will be affected by this Attinument ?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6709-flea","name":"Flea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:25:58-07:00","id":947116,"title":"","content":"It says any supernatural power that might injure them. That means any, including spells, vampire powers, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:35:03-07:00","id":947265,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Now I'm imagining a Thyrsus fighting a Promethean with Arc.<br /> <br /> The Thyrsus, after studying the Promethean for a moment calls out, &quot;Your powers are weak!&quot;<br /> The Promethean shoots a lightning. The Thyrsus blocks it with an arm.<br /> The Thyrsus looks down on his arm, then up at the Promethean, smiling. &quot;And I, am strong,&quot; he continues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:03:08-07:00","id":947636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/947102-life-4-attinument?p=947116#post947116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says any supernatural power that might injure them. That means any, including spells, vampire powers, whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tend to agree with you, but I wonder if this was the will of the Devs. The first part of the rule goes in conflict with the second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6709-flea","name":"Flea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:07:01-07:00","id":947638,"title":"","content":"I don't see any conflict in the rules, so you're going to have to explain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T04:53:25-07:00","id":947672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/947102-life-4-attinument?p=947638#post947638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any conflict in the rules, so you're going to have to explain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first part of the rule says that this power is relevant in cases of direct modification of the mages body ( the rules referes to effect that &quot;changes&quot; the body ).<br /> Later the rules says that is applicable against every source that Injure the mage.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the Devs wanted to make this Attinument work only on effect that modifiy the body directly ( some of witch can injure the mage too ), like a Life3 Direfct Damage Spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> Talking about my opinion now, not about the rules as written, seems strange to me that, for example, a power that damage you by changing the density of the air around you could be affacted by this attinument ( and a clash of will against such kind of effect doesn`t seems appropriate to me ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6709-flea","name":"Flea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:03:02-07:00","id":947677,"title":"","content":"It's only strange that the attainment doesn't work on natural sources of damage too. That it's easier to shoot a Life Mage than mangle them with ghost Numina or whatever.<br /> <br /> Still, if it didn't change in the errata then it's probably working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:06:45-07:00","id":948728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/947102-life-4-attinument?p=947677#post947677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only strange that the attainment doesn't work on natural sources of damage too. That it's easier to shoot a Life Mage than mangle them with ghost Numina or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life's already exceptionally generous with its 4 dot attainment. The other similar attainments, Death, Fate and Forces each only protect against either mundane or supernatural phenomena. Not both. <br /> <br /> Also clash of wills versus damage isn't really a mechanical concept that exists anywhere I've seen in Chronicles. Clash of Wills is usually against tilts, conditions or narrative effects.<br /> <br /> Life 4 does however protect you against a person deliberately shooting part of your body to disable it. Your protection against being shot as damage comes from Life 2, so you don't really need it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:58:08-07:00","id":948782,"title":"","content":"Oh! Yeah, forgot about that, good point. The world makes sense again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}